  "blocks": {
    "\"Diff. The summary said it deleted dead code — turned out the function was called from a generated file.\"": "“读了 diff。摘要说删除的是死代码，结果那个函数其实被生成文件调用了。”",
    "\"I human-reviewed the AFK output.\"": "“我对 AFK 输出做了人工审查。”",
    "\"You read the diff or just the summary?\"": "“你读了 diff，还是只看了摘要？”",
    "Agents raise the volume of code produced, so review becomes the bottleneck. One useful idea is layering different review strategies. Automated checks catch the mechanical failures, automated review catches the describable ones, and human review is reserved for what only you can judge — whether the change is the right change, whether the approach fits the codebase, whether this should exist at all.": "智能体提高了代码产量，因此审查会成为瓶颈。一种有效思路是分层使用不同审查策略。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/automated-check\">自动化检查</a>捕获机械性故障，<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/automated-review\">自动化审查</a>发现能够明确描述的问题，人工审查则保留给只有你能判断的内容——这项改动是否正确、方案是否适合代码库，以及它是否根本就不该存在。",
    "Avoid: \"code review\" alone — ambiguous between human and automated.": "<em>避免：</em>只说“代码审查”，因为无法区分人工审查还是自动化审查。",
    "Review is also cheaper earlier. Reading a plan before work starts, or a small diff mid-flight, takes minutes; excavating a finished branch after an AFK run takes longer. Where you place the review checkpoint is a human-in-the-loop decision, not an afterthought.": "审查越早，成本也越低。在工作开始前阅读计划，或在过程中查看一份小 diff，只需几分钟；一次 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/afk\">AFK</a> 运行结束后再挖掘完整分支，则耗时得多。把审查节点放在哪里，是一项<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/human-in-the-loop\">人工介入</a>决策，而不是事后才考虑的问题。",
    "The user reading the code the agent produced and forming a judgement on it. Reading the diff or the changed files counts; reading the agent's description of what it did does not — narration is not the artifact. The description is a secondary source, written by the party being reviewed; the diff is the primary source, and review means reading it.": "人工审查是用户阅读<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>生成的代码并作出判断。阅读 diff 或被修改的文件才算审查；只阅读智能体对自己工作的描述不算——叙述不是产物。描述是由被审查方自己编写的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/secondary-source\">二手来源</a>；diff 才是<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/primary-source\">一手来源</a>，审查意味着真正阅读它。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
